            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
            ends up being (classical, Heyting, discrete, residue, et cetera).
          %p
            The definition of the Euclidean domain further bifurcates in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            due to the disjunctive condition above. These statements, which are equivalent in the presence of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
